-- The Reg CF regulative spine, drawn.
--
-- This is the fourth BPMN fixture, and unlike `offering.l4` — which says of
-- itself that it is "a fixture ..., not a formalisation of 17 CFR 227" and whose
-- figures are illustrative — every party, act, deadline and terminating
-- condition here is taken from the real corpus at
-- `jl4/examples/legal/regcf/regcf.l4`, whose §7 spine this mirrors line for
-- line (regcf.l4:499-573, :488-497, :619-625).
--
-- ===========================================================================
-- WHY THIS FILE EXISTS AT ALL, AND WHAT IT COSTS
-- ===========================================================================
--
-- The corpus CANNOT be exported to BPMN today, and this file is the workaround,
-- not the fix. `L4.StateGraph.findRegulativeExpr` peels only `Where` and
-- `LetIn` on its way to a `Regulative`:
--
--     findRegulativeExpr expr = case expr of
--       Regulative{} -> Just expr
--       RAnd{}       -> Just expr
--       ROr{}        -> Just expr
--       Where _ e _  -> findRegulativeExpr e
--       LetIn _ _ e  -> findRegulativeExpr e
--       _            -> Nothing
--
-- All three of the corpus's regulative rules are `IfThenElse`-headed — the
-- guard is written OUTSIDE the deontic head, because that is how the CFR reads
-- ("unless such securities are transferred: ...") — so `extractStateGraphs`
-- returns `[]` on `regcf.l4` and `l4 export --to=bpmn` refuses with "No
-- regulative rules found in module". Verified, not inferred:
--
--     $ l4 state-graph jl4/examples/legal/regcf/regcf.l4
--     No regulative rules found in module
--
-- So the guard is hoisted here, from the `IF` into `PROVIDED`, and the
-- corpus's two-armed `IF ... THEN <deonton> ELSE <deonton>` becomes a `ROR` of
-- two guarded obligations. THAT IS NOT THE SAME CONSTRUCT. `ROR` in L4 is a
-- choice the obliged party makes; an `IF` is a branch the facts make. They
-- coincide here only because the two `PROVIDED` guards are exact complements,
-- so exactly one arm is ever applicable. A reader who takes the drawn
-- exclusive gateway to mean "the issuer picks one" has been misled by the
-- re-expression and not by the law.
--
-- ===========================================================================
-- WHAT THE READER SHOULD LOOK FOR IN THE GOLDENS
-- ===========================================================================
--
--   * `the ongoing reporting obligation` — the annual renewal is RECURSIVE
--     (`HENCE` back into itself with one fewer cycle). `classifyTarget` has no
--     case for an application with arguments, so the back-edge is never built;
--     the loop surfaces as a state literally named `next` with no outgoing
--     transition. `P-CYCLE` exists for exactly this and CANNOT fire, because
--     the cycle never reaches the state graph to be detected. See the fidelity
--     report: what you get instead is `P-DANGLING`.
--   * every deadline is a NAME, not a number, because the corpus binds each
--     period once (`regcf.l4:123-146`) and every consumer reads the binding.
--     That is the single-sourcing the whole programme argues for, and it is
--     precisely what stops BPMN drawing a timer: `P-DEADLINE` on every
--     boundary event. Inlining `5` and `120` here would produce prettier
--     diagrams by reintroducing the duplication the corpus exists to remove.
--   * `the resale restriction` and `the advertising restriction` are
--     prohibitions, and BPMN has no shape for "you may not". Both are drawn as
--     tasks, with `F1` at Blocking severity saying so, and the boundary event
--     is the COMPLIANCE arm rather than the failure arm.
--
-- Fixture for `jl4/tests/BpmnExport.hs`.

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Issuer
    Intermediary
    Investor
    Purchaser

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    `file a Form C-AR annual report`
    `file a Form C-TR termination of reporting`
    `advertise the terms of the offering`
    `transfer the securities`

-- regcf.l4:129-146 — the periods, bound once.
@ref 17 CFR 227.202(a) and 227.203(b)(1) — annual report deadline
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days to file the annual report after fiscal year end` MEANS 120

@ref 17 CFR 227.203(b)(3) — Form C-TR deadline
GIVETH A NUMBER
`business days to file Form C-TR` MEANS 5

@ref 17 CFR 227.501(a) — resale restricted period
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days in the resale restricted period` MEANS 365

-- regcf.l4:113-121 — the two Rule 202(b) thresholds.
@ref 17 CFR 227.202(b)(2) — holders-of-record threshold, 300, effective 2016-05-16
GIVETH A NUMBER
`holders of record threshold` MEANS 300

@ref 17 CFR 227.202(b)(3) — total-assets threshold, $10,000,000, effective 2016-05-16
GIVETH A NUMBER
`total assets threshold` MEANS 10000000

-- ===========================================================================
-- 7. Ongoing reporting — Rules 202, 203(b). Mirrors regcf.l4:499-573.
-- ===========================================================================

@ref 17 CFR 227.202(b)
DECLARE ReportingStatus HAS
    `the issuer is required to file reports under section 13(a) or section 15(d) of the Exchange Act`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `annual reports filed since the most recent sale of securities pursuant to this part`              IS A NUMBER
    `holders of record`                                                                                IS A NUMBER
    `total assets`                                                                                     IS A NUMBER
    `the issuer or another party has repurchased all of the securities issued in reliance on section 4(a)(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the issuer has liquidated or dissolved its business in accordance with state law`                 IS A BOOLEAN

@ref 17 CFR 227.202(b)(1)
GIVEN status IS A ReportingStatus
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`(b)(1) — became an Exchange Act reporting company` status MEANS
    status's `the issuer is required to file reports under section 13(a) or section 15(d) of the Exchange Act`

@ref 17 CFR 227.202(b)(2)
GIVEN status IS A ReportingStatus
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`(b)(2) — one annual report filed and fewer than 300 holders of record` status MEANS
        status's `annual reports filed since the most recent sale of securities pursuant to this part` AT LEAST 1
    AND status's `holders of record` LESS THAN `holders of record threshold`

@ref 17 CFR 227.202(b)(3)
GIVEN status IS A ReportingStatus
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`(b)(3) — three annual reports filed and total assets not exceeding $10,000,000` status MEANS
        status's `annual reports filed since the most recent sale of securities pursuant to this part` AT LEAST 3
    AND status's `total assets` AT MOST `total assets threshold`

@ref 17 CFR 227.202(b)(4)
GIVEN status IS A ReportingStatus
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`(b)(4) — all securities repurchased` status MEANS
    status's `the issuer or another party has repurchased all of the securities issued in reliance on section 4(a)(6)`

@ref 17 CFR 227.202(b)(5)
GIVEN status IS A ReportingStatus
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`(b)(5) — liquidated or dissolved` status MEANS
    status's `the issuer has liquidated or dissolved its business in accordance with state law`

@ref 17 CFR 227.202(b)
GIVEN status IS A ReportingStatus
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a terminating condition in Rule 202(b) has occurred` status MEANS
       `(b)(1) — became an Exchange Act reporting company` status
    OR `(b)(2) — one annual report filed and fewer than 300 holders of record` status
    OR `(b)(3) — three annual reports filed and total assets not exceeding $10,000,000` status
    OR `(b)(4) — all securities repurchased` status
    OR `(b)(5) — liquidated or dissolved` status

-- regcf.l4:558-573, with the guard hoisted out of the `IF` and into `PROVIDED`
-- so that `findRegulativeExpr` can see the deontic head. `annual cycles` bounds
-- the unrolling so the residual is finite; the BPMN loses the bound along with
-- the loop.
@ref 17 CFR 227.202(a); 227.203(b)(1); 227.203(b)(3)
GIVEN status          IS A ReportingStatus
      `annual cycles` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`the ongoing reporting obligation` status `annual cycles` MEANS
        (PARTY Issuer
           MUST `file a Form C-TR termination of reporting`
           PROVIDED `a terminating condition in Rule 202(b) has occurred` status
           WITHIN `business days to file Form C-TR`
           HENCE FULFILLED
           LEST BREACH BY Issuer BECAUSE "no Form C-TR was filed within five business days of the terminating event")
   ROR  (PARTY Issuer
           MUST `file a Form C-AR annual report`
           PROVIDED NOT (`a terminating condition in Rule 202(b) has occurred` status)
           WITHIN `days to file the annual report after fiscal year end`
           HENCE `the ongoing reporting obligation` status (`annual cycles` MINUS 1)
           LEST BREACH BY Issuer BECAUSE "no Form C-AR was filed within 120 days of fiscal year end")

-- ===========================================================================
-- 6. Advertising restrictions — Rule 204(a)(1). Mirrors regcf.l4:488-497.
-- ===========================================================================

@ref 17 CFR 227.204(b)
DECLARE AdvertisingNotice HAS
    `directs investors to the intermediary's platform`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `includes information beyond that permitted by paragraph (b)`  IS A BOOLEAN

@ref 17 CFR 227.204(b)(1)-(3)
GIVEN notice IS AN AdvertisingNotice
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the notice complies with Rule 204(b)` notice MEANS
        notice's `directs investors to the intermediary's platform`
    AND NOT notice's `includes information beyond that permitted by paragraph (b)`

-- The corpus writes this as `IF complies THEN FULFILLED ELSE PARTY Issuer
-- SHANT ...`. Hoisted the same way: the exception becomes the negation of the
-- prohibition's own guard.
@ref 17 CFR 227.204(a)(1)
GIVEN notice IS AN AdvertisingNotice
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`the advertising restriction` notice MEANS
    PARTY Issuer
      SHANT `advertise the terms of the offering`
      PROVIDED NOT (`the notice complies with Rule 204(b)` notice)
      WITHIN `days in the resale restricted period`

-- ===========================================================================
-- 8. Resale restrictions — Rule 501(a). Mirrors regcf.l4:619-625.
-- ===========================================================================

@ref 17 CFR 227.501(a)
DECLARE Transfer HAS
    `is to the issuer of the securities`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `is to an accredited investor`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `is as part of an offering registered with the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a family, trust, death or divorce transfer`            IS A BOOLEAN

@ref 17 CFR 227.501(a)(1)-(4)
GIVEN transfer IS A Transfer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the transfer falls within an exception in Rule 501(a)` transfer MEANS
       transfer's `is to the issuer of the securities`
    OR transfer's `is to an accredited investor`
    OR transfer's `is as part of an offering registered with the Commission`
    OR transfer's `is a family, trust, death or divorce transfer`

@ref 17 CFR 227.501(a)
GIVEN transfer IS A Transfer
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`the resale restriction` transfer MEANS
    PARTY Purchaser
      SHANT `transfer the securities`
      PROVIDED NOT (`the transfer falls within an exception in Rule 501(a)` transfer)
      WITHIN `days in the resale restricted period`
